4b-a304-ec0efb6d37ff" :question/math-academy-id "q-98701" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071359/assets/74790c4dbcb2d9cebee802dd155b5fa0a94e442f9bbc59c6277eb0d6fca3d60a.png)\n\nA particular autonomous differential equation has the phase line shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $y=-2$ is a source\n- $y=-5$ is a node\n- $y=-5$ is a sink" :question/worked-solution "We can classify the equilibrium solutions of an autonomous ODE ${y}^{′}=f(y)$ by examining its phase line.\n\n- An equilibrium solution is a *sink* if the arrows directly above and below it on the phase line both point *toward* the equilibrium solution.\n\n- An equilibrium solution is a *source* if the arrows directly above and below it on the phase line both point *away* from the equilibrium solution.\n\n- An equilibrium solution is a *node* if the arrows directly above and below it on the phase line point in the same direction.\n\nLet's check each statement:\n\n- Statement I is true. Notice that the arrow just above the point $y=-2$ points upward, and the arrow just below it points downward. In other words, both arrows point *away* from  $y=-2.$ This means that $y=-2$ is a source.\n\n- Statement II is false, while statement III is true. Notice that the arrow just above the point $y=-5$ points downward, and the arrow just below it points upward. In other words, both arrows point *toward* the point $y=-5.$ This means that $y=-5$ is a sink.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-98701/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "680a42fd-9b70-5fb2-916c-d10b71b11d82"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-98701"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-339664"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/140