validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-98715"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071359/assets/4a2c0103fb348883b05692721162ffba17758beb0e6f944deb328a506fed8d21.png)\n\nConsiderer the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(y)$ where the graph of $f(y)$ is shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $y=4$ is a source.\n- $y=2$ is a node.\n- $y=-1$ is a sink." :question/worked-solution "We can classify the equilibrium solutions of an autonomous ODE ${y}^{′}=f(y)$ by examining its phase line.\n\n- An equilibrium solution is a *sink* if the arrows directly above and below it on the phase line both point *toward* the equilibrium solution.\n\n- An equilibrium solution is a *source* if the arrows directly above and below it on the phase line both point *away* from the equilibrium solution.\n\n- An equilibrium solution is a *node* if the arrows directly above and below it on the phase line point in the same direction.\n\nThe phase line that corresponds to the given graph is as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071359/assets/df340c40982e6d22ef8a815bf043f84fd78b43b4ddc1763845d03d4b2c793aee.png)\n\nTherefore, we have:\n\n- Statement I is false. From the phase line, we see that $y=4$ is a sink.\n\n- Statement II is false. From the phase line, we see that $y=2$ is a source.\n\n- Statement III is true. From the phase line, we see that $y=-1$ is a sink.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only\"." :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-339711/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "5fd8f14d-2fc8-549a-8b79-a766a644a134" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339711/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "52c0b255-d908-5577-9904-274eb32